[2026-08-23T01:00+00:00] {
  "methodology": "Candidate leads were gathered from the supplied inventories and then filtered for public, non-fork, non-archived repositories with material in-repository GPU-kernel or closely adjacent technology. Qualification required direct repository code or documentation showing CUDA C/C++, Triton, CUTLASS/CuTe, GPU compiler/code-generation, communication primitives, memory infrastructure, benchmarking, profiling, debugging, instrumentation, or GPU simulation work. Canonical identity, exact stargazers_count, description, archived/fork status, and pushed_at were required from a live GitHub REST repository endpoint observed on 2026-08-23. Redirects and names were normalized case-insensitively, pushed_at was reduced to a date, and eligible records were ordered by exact stars descending with canonical owner/name ascending as the tie-breaker.",
  "cutoff_notes": "No defensible 100th-place cutoff can be reported. The completed research and follow-up audit produced only 58 unique replacement-quality eligible records after deduplication; several of the seven follow-up records duplicated repositories already present, with pytorch/FBGEMM being the sole new unique addition. The remaining supplied leads contain approximate or stale stars, missing pushed_at values, unresolved redirects, absent current code evidence, archived/superseded projects, dependency-only wrappers, or merely incidental CUDA use. Archived projects were excluded rather than used as padding. Because 58 is less than 100, declaring a 100th-place star threshold, near-miss ordering, or another 42 finalists would require fabrication or presentation of unverified metadata as live verification. GitHub stars are also inherently a time-sensitive snapshot.",
  "repos": [],
  "audit_summary": "The requested final artifact cannot be truthfully emitted from tasks 4, 5, and 6. Mechanical audit result: required array length 100 — FAIL (only 58 unique replacement-quality eligible repositories were established); 100 unique canonical repositories and URLs — FAIL; ranks 1 through 100 — FAIL; every required field populated for 100 records — FAIL; nonempty direct-source lists for 100 records — FAIL; fork=false and archived=false for all 100 — not testable beyond the verified subset; monotonically non-increasing exact stars across 100 records — not testable. Consequently repos is intentionally empty rather than presenting a partial array as a completed top 100 or fabricating 42 repositories. A compliant result requires at least 42 additional direct GitHub metadata and current-tree verifications, followed by complete reranking and another mechanical audit."
}
